  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-user-rules — User rules settings page",
      "text": "[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@railgun52/dsh-user-rules)\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n> A profile-config settings page for DeepSeek Harness that injects your own development rules into every session's system prompt."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-user-rules — User rules settings page",
      "text": "Rules you add here are concatenated into a `user-rules` systemPrompt section, so the model obeys them on the next turn — edit and it takes effect without a restart. The page is a list editor over the `user-rules` profile-config namespace; the Host half owns the schema and the systemPrompt section, the browser half owns the editor card."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "| Feature | Description |\n|---|---|\n| Settings page | A first-level Settings section `用户规则` with add/edit/remove/reorder card list |\n| systemPrompt injection | The resolved `rules` become a numbered systemPrompt section named `user-rules` (order `-50`) |\n| Live edits | `rules` is declared `.volatile()`; the section text reads the live value at assembly time, so new turns pick up edits with no remount |\n| Profile-config backed | Values persist to the active profile's plugin config; the page reads/writes through the shared `configForms` namespace |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "```text\ndsh-user-rules/\n|-- src/\n|   |-- index.ts               # host half: Config schema (volatile rules) + systemPrompt section\n|   |-- user-rules-schema.ts   # UserRulesSchema"
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "- **Namespace**: `user-rules`. The owning profile entry id must equal this string; the plugin's Config schema IS the namespace under the profile-config settings model.\n- **Injection**: `apply` registers a `systemPrompt.section` whose `text` reads `config.rules.get()` on every assembly, so the rules always reflect the current value.\n- **Browser bundle**: rides the `window.__ModuleLoader__.load` contract; React and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives` resolve from the loader's module table (external); CSS Modules are inlined by lightningcss as `<style data-plugin>`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "From a local directory (development)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add link:/absolute/path/to/dsh-user-rules"
    },
    {
      "section": "From npm (recommended)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add @railgun52/dsh-user-rules@latest\n```\n\nAfter installing, **restart `dsh web`**. Open Settings → 用户规则 to manage rules. In link mode, run `pnpm build` and refresh the page after a code change; no reinstall needed."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install\npnpm build        # tsc -b (types+declarations) && tsdown (node half + browser bundle)\npnpm typecheck    # type check only\n```\n\nThe browser bundle is produced with the harness `clientBundle` helper; building from a fresh clone requires the DeepSeek Harness repository available (the `tsdown.config.ts` imports its `clientBundle`). The shipped `lib/` is pre-built, so consumers never build."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
  ],
